# --- Generated output ---------------------------------------------------------------
# Rebuilt from source by CI and the Dockerfile; reformatting it is pure noise.
ui/dist
pkg/server/ui-dist
**/node_modules

# --- Lock files ---------------------------------------------------------------------
pnpm-lock.yaml
package-lock.json

# --- Markdown -----------------------------------------------------------------------
# Every .md file carries a "Last Updated / Last Reviewed" footer, and CI cross-checks it
# against git's real last-modified date for that file (scripts/check_docs_review.py
# --changed-files). Reformatting all 35 docs would mark every one of them modified and
# demand a footer bump on each, turning a formatting pass into a documentation review.
*.md

# --- HTML ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Server-rendered pages and the localised email templates. Prettier reflows HTML, and
# whitespace between inline elements is rendered, so this can change layout and how mail
# clients display a message. Not worth the risk for formatting alone.
*.html

# --- Workflows and other YAML -------------------------------------------------------
# ci.yml carries long explanatory comments whose indentation Prettier reflows, and a
# mangled workflow is a broken merge gate rather than an ugly file.
*.yml
*.yaml

# --- Canonical shared docs files ----------------------------------------------------
# This repo holds the CANONICAL copy of four files shared by the three Liferay tools docs
# sites (LDM, AICA, lfr-tunnel; #2391, #2397). LDM and AICA are to copy them, and their
# docs CI is to fail unless their copy has the same content as this repo's master -- LDM
# may keep the hook at a different path (sync plan: AICA #1329). Once those checks exist,
# Prettier rewriting any of these here would fail all of them at once: a formatting change
# that reads as upstream drift. Keep all four listed by name. The two templates are also
# matched by *.html above, but that glob exists for unrelated reasons and must not be what
# protects them. The .py hook is outside Prettier's scope today; it is listed so this
# block stays the complete set.
docs/assets/stylesheets/liferay-blue.css
scripts/mkdocs_github_alerts.py
overrides/main.html
overrides/partials/copyright.html
